00:10:44.543 --> 00:10:45.877
There was no plan in place.

00:10:45.877 --> 00:10:47.646
You didn't even buy enough
when you had the chance.

00:10:47.646 --> 00:10:49.949
What did you do besides,
say, make a vaccine?

00:10:49.949 --> 00:10:52.684
I can't imagine you tinkering
and the lab saying

00:10:52.684 --> 00:10:56.021
we should use an MRNA platform
instead of an adenovirus.

00:10:56.021 --> 00:10:59.124
I mean, if Trump ever even saw
the word MRNA,

00:10:59.124 --> 00:11:01.326
he'd probably think
it was a guy named Mr. Nah.

00:11:01.326 --> 00:11:05.097
We're working very hard with
Mr. Na to produce more vaccines.

00:11:05.097 --> 00:11:10.335
Mr. Na, bad guy. Mean guy.
A nice to me, though. Loves me.

00:11:10.335 --> 00:11:11.870
So the Conservative Political
Action Conference

00:11:11.870 --> 00:11:13.338
revealed yet again

00:11:13.338 --> 00:11:15.207
that the modern conservative
movement is a personality cult,

00:11:15.207 --> 00:11:17.109
fostering a sociopathic
political culture

00:11:17.109 --> 00:11:18.477
of paranoia
and conspiracy theories

00:11:18.477 --> 00:11:20.880
that's fully unmoored
from reality.

00:11:20.880 --> 00:11:23.548
At one point, Donald Trump
Junior even suggested

00:11:23.548 --> 00:11:24.783
a more accurate name

00:11:24.783 --> 00:11:27.152
would be the Trump
Political Action Conference.

00:11:27.152 --> 00:11:28.987
-How's it going, CPAC?

00:11:28.987 --> 00:11:31.457
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:11:31.457 --> 00:11:33.692
Or I heard someone earlier
phrase it

00:11:33.692 --> 00:11:37.196
a little bit better,
T-PAC.

00:11:37.196 --> 00:11:39.932
It's what it feels like, guys.

00:11:39.932 --> 00:11:41.934
T-PAC?

00:11:41.934 --> 00:11:44.537
Even they didn't know
what to do with that.

00:11:44.537 --> 00:11:45.805
You couldn't think
of anything lamer?

00:11:45.805 --> 00:11:49.441
I think T-PAC is the name
of a pink-eye medication

00:11:49.441 --> 00:11:53.011
T-PAC sounds like the name
of an off brand Tupac hologram

00:11:53.011 --> 00:11:55.847
at a festival that couldn't get
the rights to use his real name.

00:11:55.847 --> 00:11:57.583
Welcome to
the Couchella Festival.

00:11:57.583 --> 00:12:00.052
Please welcome T-PAC,
singing his classic song,

00:12:00.052 --> 00:12:01.620
"California Hugs."

00:12:01.620 --> 00:12:03.421
Then at another point
Kimberly Guilfoyle suggested

00:12:03.421 --> 00:12:05.724
Trump would accomplish more
as an ex-president

00:12:05.724 --> 00:12:08.594
than Biden would accomplish
as the actual president.

00:12:08.594 --> 00:12:11.864
-I will confidently say that
President Trump from his desk

00:12:11.864 --> 00:12:14.899
at Mar-a-Lago
will accomplish more for America

00:12:14.899 --> 00:12:16.535
in the next four years

00:12:16.535 --> 00:12:21.206
than Joe Biden and Kamala Harris
could ever dream of.

00:12:21.206 --> 00:12:23.609
-Have you ever even seen him
at his desk at Mar a Lago?

00:12:23.609 --> 00:12:25.410
He looks like a tourist posing
for a photo

00:12:25.410 --> 00:12:27.680
at Letterman's old desk.
Just holding a pen

00:12:27.680 --> 00:12:29.581
and what appears to be
an empty notepad,

00:12:29.581 --> 00:12:31.350
like a therapist who hasn't been
paying attention

00:12:31.350 --> 00:12:33.418
during the session.
And yet, the conference

00:12:33.418 --> 00:12:35.854
also proved that Trump
is also as politically weak

00:12:35.854 --> 00:12:38.623
as he's ever been among the hard
core Republicans at CPAC.

00:12:38.623 --> 00:12:40.893
He only got 55 percent
of the vote in a straw poll

00:12:40.893 --> 00:12:42.794
and only 68 percent
want him to run again.

00:12:42.794 --> 00:12:46.265
If you can't even get above
55 percent with these wingnuts,

00:12:46.265 --> 00:12:48.367
how could you ever get a
majority in a national election?

00:12:48.367 --> 00:12:49.868
This is your crowd.

00:12:49.868 --> 00:12:51.670
It's like if you open a store
that sells monocles

00:12:51.670 --> 00:12:53.372
in artisanal pickles
in Williamsburg,

00:12:53.372 --> 00:12:54.706
if you don't make
a killing there,

00:12:54.706 --> 00:12:57.109
you're not going to do better
in, like, Staten Island.

00:12:57.109 --> 00:12:59.111
But the only truly
unifying thing at CPAC,

00:12:59.111 --> 00:13:00.846
the beating heart
of modern conservatism,

00:13:00.846 --> 00:13:04.683
where the dumb invented culture,
war grievances is evidenced

00:13:04.683 --> 00:13:06.819
by their complaints
about total nonsense

00:13:06.819 --> 00:13:09.121
like "The Muppets"
and Mr. Potato Head.

00:13:09.121 --> 00:13:13.392
-This month alone,
they've banned "The Muppets."

00:13:13.392 --> 00:13:14.960
-You see,
last week they tried to cancel

00:13:14.960 --> 00:13:17.629
Kermit the Frog and Mr. Potato
Head? You see that?

00:13:17.629 --> 00:13:20.966
-Look out, Mr. Potato Head.
You're next.

00:13:20.966 --> 00:13:24.469
-I mean, I guess I would be
concerned about Mr. Potato Head

00:13:24.469 --> 00:13:28.607
if I answer to Mr. Blockhead,
I mean, Matt Gaetz's,

00:13:28.607 --> 00:13:31.610
head has sharper corners
than military sheets.

00:13:31.610 --> 00:13:34.246
Also, that's really
what you think Americans care

00:13:34.246 --> 00:13:36.782
about amid a pandemic,
and economic crash?

00:13:36.782 --> 00:13:38.116
"The Muppets"
and Mr. Potato Head?

00:13:38.116 --> 00:13:40.152
My kids don't even care
about "The Muppets"

00:13:40.152 --> 00:13:41.419
and Mr. Potato Head.

00:13:41.419 --> 00:13:42.921
They want to watch Fortnite
streams on Twitch.

00:13:42.921 --> 00:13:45.090
Even though I have been trying
to get them into the new online

00:13:45.090 --> 00:13:48.226
Ocean Master, you get tiles
for every reef you explore

00:13:48.226 --> 00:13:50.929
and then you use the tiles
to build islands to mine ore.

00:13:50.929 --> 00:13:52.464
And whoever mines the most ore
gets to control

00:13:52.464 --> 00:13:56.435
the wurfel,
which is German for dice.

00:13:56.435 --> 00:13:59.070
It's fun!

00:13:59.070 --> 00:14:00.505
The Conservative
Political Action Conference

00:14:00.505 --> 00:14:02.407
revealed once again that the
modern conservative movement

00:14:02.407 --> 00:14:04.543
remains totally detached
from reality

00:14:04.543 --> 00:14:06.044
and the mainstream
American politics.

00:14:06.044 --> 00:14:08.647
People care about the pandemic
and the economic crash.

00:14:08.647 --> 00:14:11.316
But at CPAC, they're obsessed
with lies about the election.

00:14:11.316 --> 00:14:12.952
Mr. Potato Head
and "The Muppets."

00:14:12.952 --> 00:14:15.654
And yet still, Trump couldn't
crack 55 percent

00:14:15.654 --> 00:14:18.090
when Trump heard
he only got 55 percent.

00:14:18.090 --> 00:14:21.059
He must have been like.
-Oh! [ Yells ]

00:14:21.059 --> 00:14:25.096
-Stop!
-Oh!

